        "original_id": "b87ff838-9b0a-5b8b-8fad-80c72021c499",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Ships: San Juan de Sicilia\n- Events: Spanish Armada of 1588\n- People: Duke of Medina Sidonia\n- Places: La Coruña, Flanders, England\n\nFacts:\n- The Spanish Armada of 1588 was a Spanish fleet of 130 ships.\n- In August 1588, the Spanish Armada sailed from La Coruña under the command of the Duke of Medina Sidonia.\n- The purpose of the Spanish Armada was to escort an army from Flanders to invade England.\n- The San Juan de Sicilia was one of the 130 ships in the ill-fated Spanish Armada of 1588.",
